+### Conventional distribution check
+
+The pinned distribution hook requires GNU sed's in-place/change-command syntax;
+macOS BSD sed does not accept it. GNU sed 4.10 was source-built in an owned prefix,
+verified against the [primary release announcement](https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/info-gnu/2026-04/msg00009.html).
+An equivalent local host-tool setup, from the patched source root, is:
+
+```sh
+sed_host=$(mktemp -d "$vlc_source/../vlc-sed-host.XXXXXX")
+curl --fail --location --max-time 60 --max-filesize 4000000 \
+  --output "$sed_host/sed-4.10.tar.gz" \
+  https://mirrors.kernel.org/gnu/sed/sed-4.10.tar.gz
+expected=4d179ffaf92ec4dcec541f7c032be1c3b9a1856f4970adb95a505221702f5277
+actual=$(shasum -a 256 "$sed_host/sed-4.10.tar.gz" | awk '{print $1}')
+test "$actual" = "$expected"
+tar -xzf "$sed_host/sed-4.10.tar.gz" -C "$sed_host"
+(cd "$sed_host/sed-4.10" && ./configure --prefix="$sed_host/prefix" \
+  --disable-nls && make -j4 && make install)
+export VLC_PATH="$sed_host/prefix/bin:$VLC_PATH"
+cd "$vlc_source"
+vlcSetBaseEnvironment # reconstructs PATH from VLC_PATH, not the previous PATH
+sed --version # verify GNU sed remains selected after the official environment
+export GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES="$vlc_output"
+make -C "$vlc_output" -j4 distcheck \
+  DISTCHECK_CONFIGURE_FLAGS="--host=$HOST_TRIPLET --build=$BUILD_TRIPLET --with-contrib=$vlc_output/contrib/$HOST_TRIPLET --disable-macosx"
+```
+
+The scoped [Git discovery ceiling](https://git-scm.com/docs/git/2.45.1.html)
+prevents an extracted archive from discovering an ancestor checkout and replacing
+its shipped revision. The real source checkout remains identifiable; no source
+permission or revision rule is changed. Use `set -eo pipefail`, not `set -u`, when
+sourcing the official environment because it expects optional unset variables.
+The separate leading source-header distribution patch lists five existing headers
+omitted by the pinned archive manifests; it changes no runtime code.
+
+The guarded conventional run passed archive membership/bytes, minimal configure,
+platform compilation and linking, then failed during runtime tests. The main test
+directory reported 92 tests: 80 pass, five skip, seven fail. Failures were clock
+drift, decoder subpicture, SPU creation, TLS certificate/handshake, unavailable BMP
+encoding, OpenGL operation and CVPX conversion. Relevant source/test bytes remain
+identical to the pin; causes are not all established. A bounded untouched-master
+normal-configuration comparison reproduced the clock drift_72 and TLS tls.c:188
+failures. That full baseline configuration differs from minimal distcheck, and the
+selected TLS client cause remains unproven. Upstream minimal flags disable
+avcodec/swscale, and this profile separately disables the helper and macOS GUI.
+Install/installcheck/uninstall/DESTDIR cleanup/redist/distclean stages were not
+reached: conventional distcheck is not qualified. No tests were disabled to force
+a pass. This remains separate from the feature-enabled app/helper/XCTest proofs.
+
+Preserved failures include the initial unset-variable launcher, BSD sed hook,
+pre-environment PATH placement, ancestor Git revision discovery and missing Apple/
+medialibrary archive headers. Generated gettext translation deltas and failed
+archives are preserved separately from the proposed source series. Host fixes and
+manifest prerequisites do not erase that execution history.
 
